# =============================================================================
# DOCUMENTATION HEADER — Monolithic Planner — user prompt template
# =============================================================================
# This header is documentation for maintainers. The runtime loader reads the
# entire file (including these lines) into the LLM prompt string. Keep the
# original instructional sections below unchanged in meaning and order.
#
# SECTION: Placeholders
#   {goals_context} and {agent_context} filled by MonolithicPlanner.plan().
#
# SECTION: Sequencing rules
#   No parallelism; first task empty deps; later tasks use zero-based indices.
#
# SECTION: Index note
#   dependency_task_ids are planner-local indices remapped by save_plan_to_db.
#
# =============================================================================
{goals_context}

{agent_context}

Generate a sequential plan that addresses all the goals above.
Tasks from different goals can be interleaved, but NO parallelism is allowed.
Each task should depend on the previous task(s).

For the first task, use an empty dependency_task_ids list.
For subsequent tasks, make each depend on relevant previous tasks.

Important: Since task IDs will be assigned by the database, in your dependency_task_ids,
use zero-based indices that represent the position of the task in your tasks array
(e.g., task at index 1 depends on task at index 0, so dependency_task_ids = [0]). 